you dirty little bastard"?

12:26.931 --> 12:28.097
Sorry, I'll take that.

12:28.132 --> 12:30.299
Here's your cake.
I ate a great deal of it.

12:35.773 --> 12:36.806
Oh, there you are.

12:36.841 --> 12:38.574
How was your first
day out of rehab?

12:38.610 --> 12:40.009
It was terrible.

12:40.044 --> 12:41.844
Taking that class
made no difference.

12:41.879 --> 12:44.013
Nobody wants anything
to do with me.

12:44.048 --> 12:45.214
Hi, Mr. Herbert.

12:45.249 --> 12:46.215
Oh, my God.

12:46.250 --> 12:47.216
Children, run!

12:47.251 --> 12:48.618
It's that pervert!

12:48.653 --> 12:51.153
Everybody into my
safety basement!

12:51.189 --> 12:53.456
Oh! Oh, that
was a bad snap.

12:53.491 --> 12:54.890
I'm hurt, kids!

12:54.926 --> 12:57.927
Don't eat those popsicles
till I get down there!

13:02.667 --> 13:05.067
Well, I'm glad we're finally
getting some practice in.

13:05.103 --> 13:06.636
Yeah, nothing like
running around

13:06.671 --> 13:09.105
after eating
a seafood tower.

13:09.140 --> 13:10.539
What are you
doing here?

13:10.575 --> 13:11.941
You're supposed to
be at the baseline.

13:11.976 --> 13:13.376
Yeah, baseline,
baseline.

13:13.411 --> 13:15.211
Right, right.
He's serving to you.

13:15.246 --> 13:16.312
Get back there!

13:22.453 --> 13:24.053
You've never played
tennis, have you?

13:24.088 --> 13:25.454
Not once.
Damn it, Brian!

13:25.490 --> 13:26.889
I entered us in
that tournament

13:26.924 --> 13:28.290
because you said
you could play!

13:28.326 --> 13:29.725
And I will not
be humiliated

13:29.761 --> 13:32.161
in front of shallow,
rich alcoholics!

13:36.167 --> 13:37.767
Hey, Chris.

13:37.802 --> 13:39.769
I see you walked
across the grass again

13:39.804 --> 13:41.404
instead of
using the walk.

13:41.439 --> 13:43.139
You're really wearing
a path, aren't you?

13:43.174 --> 13:44.640
We call that
Chris's Trail.

13:44.676 --> 13:45.641
Right there.

13:45.677 --> 13:47.143
Chris's Trail.

13:47.178 --> 13:49.578
Mr. Quagmire,
I completed that sex rehab

13:49.614 --> 13:51.280
and I paid my debt to society,

13:51.315 --> 13:53.983
but people are still afraid of
me, like I'm some kind of creep.

13:54.018 --> 13:55.651
How do I get them to treat me

13:55.687 --> 13:57.486
the way they did
before all this happened?

13:57.522 --> 13:59.188
You can't. I'm sorry, Chris,

13:59.223 --> 14:01.323
but you're just gonna have
to accept that from now on,

14:01.359 --> 14:03.325
people are gonna see you
as a sex-crazed pervert.

14:03.361 --> 14:05.528
And there's nothing
you can do to change that.

14:05.563 --> 14:08.364
Wait a minute,
maybe there is.

14:08.399 --> 14:09.999
Thanks, Mr. Quagmire.

14:10.034 --> 14:11.000
No problem, Chris.

14:11.035 --> 14:12.201
You keep that
chin up, huh?

14:12.236 --> 14:13.269
I will.

14:13.304 --> 14:14.837
Hey, can I ring
your doorbell?

14:14.872 --> 14:16.038
No, I'd rather you...

14:17.075 --> 14:18.474
That's why "no," Chris.

14:18.509 --> 14:19.709
That's why "no."

14:26.484 --> 14:28.851
Chris? What the hell
happened to you?

14:28.886 --> 14:30.319
Mother, Father,

14:30.354 --> 14:33.122
I decided to have myself
chemically castrated.

14:33.157 --> 14:34.724
Why the hell would
you do that?!

14:34.759 --> 14:37.159
Now nobody will have
any reason to be afraid of me

14:37.195 --> 14:38.794
or think I'm a pervert,

14:38.830 --> 14:41.797
and everybody can just
treat me like normal again.

14:41.833 --> 14:45.201
Oh, my God, I can't believe
my son's some kind of weirdo!

14:45.236 --> 14:46.669
Uh, here comes
another sandwich.

14:49.373 --> 14:51.140
I can't even look at you.

14:57.117 --> 14:59.083
Has anyone seen my sandals?

14:59.119 --> 15:00.918
Yeah, no, nobody's seen
your sandals.

15:00.954 --> 15:03.454
Well, I'll just have
to make another pair.

15:03.490 --> 15:06.457
Look, Chris, I know you
think chemical castration

15:06.493 --> 15:07.892
is gonna solve
your problems,

15:07.927 --> 15:10.461
but you have to stop
taking those pills.

15:10.497 --> 15:11.763
I don't have to do anything,

15:11.798 --> 15:14.031
besides get to the wind chime
store before it closes.

15:14.067 --> 15:15.933
There can't be
a whole store.

15:15.969 --> 15:18.336
To be fair, they also have
a couple of kaleidoscopes.

15:18.371 --> 15:19.704
Ah, can I come?

15:19.739 --> 15:21.773
Lois, can I go to the store
with that thing?

15:21.808 --> 15:25.376
Splendid. I'll go get
my burlap wallet.

15:25.411 --> 15:29.213
Wow, we rolled three gutter
balls on these kids, huh?

15:40.727 --> 15:43.127
My word, Brian,
you're really improving.

15:43.163 --> 15:44.529
We might actually
win this thing.

15:44.564 --> 15:46.164
Thanks. You know,
I just pretend

15:46.199 --> 15:47.832
that tennis ball
is Mitch McConnell

15:47.867 --> 15:50.034
trying to roll back subsidies
on the Affordable Care Act,

15:50.069 --> 15:51.536
and I'm like, "Nope!"

15:51.571 --> 15:53.538
Yeah, I-I don't... I don't
need to hear your process.

15:53.573 --> 15:54.972
Look, I'm just happy
you pushed me,

15:55.008 --> 15:56.374
'cause now I can't wait
for that tournament.

15:56.409 --> 15:58.209
I know,
it's gonna be great.

15:58.244 --> 16:01.179
And I already know exactly
where I'm gonna put that trophy.

16:01.214 --> 16:02.613
So the baby died?

16:02.649 --> 16:04.015
Yeah, the baby died.

16:04.050 --> 16:06.217
But, look, first place.

16:10.523 --> 16:13.491
Chris, your mother and I want
you to stop taking them pills.

16:13.526 --> 16:15.827
There's a lot of great things
about having a sex drive

16:15.862 --> 16:17.895
that you're missing out on.
Like what?

16:17.931 --> 16:20.565
Well, there's the post-orgy
meals at a swingers party.

16:20.600 --> 16:22.867
Come on, let's eat with
these wonderful people.

16:22.902 --> 16:25.236
Hey, everybody,
try my wife's ambrosia.

16:25.271 --> 16:28.306
If you liked my wife's snizz,
you're gonna love her ambrosia.

16:28.341 --> 16:30.308
I was thinking about
this seven-layer dip

16:30.343 --> 16:32.476
the whole time I
was chowing Ronald.

16:32.512 --> 16:33.911
I don't like this.

16:33.947 --> 16:35.346
I want to go home.

16:35.381 --> 16:36.547
You know what's sad?

16:36.583 --> 16:39.417
There's hardly any other
fathers and sons here.

16:43.489 --> 16:44.722
I don't know, Lois.

16:44.757 --> 16:46.891
I just don't think
Chris is gonna change his mind.

16:46.926 --> 16:48.326
I know.

16:48.361 --> 16:49.594
It's only a matter of time

16:49.629 --> 16:51.162
before he shaves
one side of his head

16:51.197 --> 16:53.164
and swoops the rest
of the hair over.

16:53.199 --> 16:55.499
Why, is that...
is that bad?

16:55.535 --> 16:57.602
Good early
evening, everyone.

16:57.637 --> 16:59.604
I have celebratory news.

16:59.639 --> 17:03.774
With all the free time, I'm
no longer devoting to onanism...

17:03.810 --> 17:05.610
That's spanking it?
Yes, Peter.

17:05.645 --> 17:08.446
...I have managed to redirect
that energy into my studies.

17:08.481 --> 17:11.883
In fact, today I received
the Kaplan Prize in biology.

17:11.918 --> 17:13.818
Chris, that's great!

17:13.853 --> 17:17.221
Not only that, I got the highest
score on my Spanish test,

17:17.257 --> 17:19.323
and I even joined
the debate team.

17:19.359 --> 17:21.225
That's amazing!

17:21.261 --> 17:24.228
All right, well, I'm gonna
put some flowers in a wagon

17:24.264 --> 17:26.097
and walk around town.

17:27.800 --> 17:29.200
You know what, Peter?

17:29.235 --> 17:31.569
Maybe there's a silver
lining to this fiasco.

17:31.604 --> 17:33.571
Not thinking about
sex all the time

17:33.606 --> 17:36.407
seems to have allowed Chris
to excel in other areas.

17:36.442 --> 17:37.808
He does seem sharper.

17:37.844 --> 17:39.644
Heck, the old Chris
couldn't even figure out

17:39.679 --> 17:41.646
the self-checkout
at the supermarket.

17:41.681 --> 17:44.081
Please place
the item in the bagging area.

17:44.117 --> 17:46.484
Please remove the item
from the bagging area.

17:46.519 --> 17:49.487
Please take a plastic bag
from the bagging area.

17:49.522 --> 17:51.956
Please put the bag over
your head and tighten.

17:59.799 --> 18:01.766
I told you I could
make him do it.

18:01.801 --> 18:03.000
That's hard-core, man.

18:03.036 --> 18:05.002
You're hard-core.

18:10.276 --> 18:11.909
All right, Brian,
we win this set,

18:11.945 --> 18:13.110
the tournament's ours.

18:13.146 --> 18:14.445
Yeah, come on,
let's do this.

18:14.480 --> 18:16.580
I can already see our
names in the newsletter,

18:16.616 --> 18:18.950
right below the deaths
from the previous quarter.

18:27.327 --> 18:29.160
Out.
What?!

18:29.195 --> 18:30.361
Your ball was long.

18:30.396 --> 18:31.595
Are you me?!

18:31.631 --> 18:32.797
That thing was in!

18:32.832 --> 18:34.165
You're gonna penalize us

18:34.200 --> 18:37.168
because you're a blind
blue jacket?!

18:37.203 --> 18:38.369
Stewie, calm down.

18:38.404 --> 18:40.004
I will drop you
to your knees

18:40.039 --> 18:42.006
